[
    {
        "content": "<p>Given a monoidal category <code>C</code>, I would like to define a new category <code>D</code> that has the same objects as <code>C</code> but not the same arrows (a subset of arrows in <code>C</code> with an additional property). I'm struggling to do that properly: my final purpose is to use the fact that <code>C</code> is monoidal to prove that <code>D</code> also is by reducing all goals to prove that the property of the arrows in <code>D</code> are preserved under the tensor product of <code>C</code>. Here is a small code example that summarize my problem:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CategoryTheory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalCategory</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Category</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">},</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Best way to define D?</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">D</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Category</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">D</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fails</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">id_comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">comp_id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Are there any experts in this field who know the most effective way to go about it? Thanks a lot!</p>",
        "id": 579971702,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1773759822
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Does <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Widesubcategory.html#CategoryTheory.WideSubcategory\">CategoryTheory.WideSubcategory</a> help?</p>",
        "id": 579973487,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Merten",
        "timestamp": 1773760132
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also, the way we usually deal with such property of arrows is via the wrapper <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.MorphismProperty#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.MorphismProperty</a>. It would be nice to have \"monoidal\" morphisms properties.</p>",
        "id": 579973982,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Carlier",
        "timestamp": 1773760219
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We have <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Localization/Monoidal/Basic.html#CategoryTheory.MorphismProperty.IsMonoidal\">CategoryTheory.MorphismProperty.IsMonoidal</a>, I don't know if this is what you have in mind though.</p>",
        "id": 579974267,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Merten",
        "timestamp": 1773760269
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Indeed <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.WideSubcategory#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.WideSubcategory</a> seems to be a nice way to go. And <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Localization/Monoidal/Basic.html#CategoryTheory.MorphismProperty.IsMonoidal\">CategoryTheory.MorphismProperty.IsMonoidal</a> seems very promising. Maybe it is enough to show the latter on my property for <code>WideSubcategory P</code> to be monoidal.</p>",
        "id": 579974874,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1773760378
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><del>Maybe <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Localization/Monoidal/Basic.html#CategoryTheory.Localization.Monoidal.instMonoidalCategoryLocalizedMonoidal\">instMonoidalCategoryLocalizedMonoidal</a>.</del></p>",
        "id": 579976267,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1773760694
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You will most likely have to define the <code>MonoidalCategoryStruct</code> on the <code>WideSubcategory</code> by hand.</p>",
        "id": 579979933,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Carlier",
        "timestamp": 1773761542
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You may try using <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.Monoidal.induced#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.Monoidal.induced</a></p>",
        "id": 580003929,
        "sender_full_name": "Joël Riou",
        "timestamp": 1773767010
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thank you for the suggestion, <del>unfortunately in my case I cannot construct a functor from <code>D</code> to <code>C</code> but that's a nice reference to have in mind. I ended up following <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"286014\">@Robin Carlier</span>'s advice and constructed <code>MonoidalCategoryStruct</code> by hand (it basically reduces to show that my <code>MorphismProperty</code> is stable by tensor product, whiskers and unitors). The other axioms come for free using <code>WideSubcategory</code>.</del></p>",
        "id": 580005235,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1773767363
    }
]